        {
          "type": "datasheet",
          "title": "Technical data",
          "note": "TEI’s technical specifications assume a 40% hydraulic power loss.",
          "tagline": "Drill rig for confined spaces",
          "intro": [
            "TEI manufactures the TD75, an electrically driven drill rig for confined spaces, designed to safely and quietly install micropiles and grout holes. All models of TEI’s patented drifters and rotary heads can be combined with the TD75 electric track drill.",
            "The wide range of electric drilling solutions makes the confined-space rigs perfect for working through narrow or low entrances and exits, under buildings and in tunnels and mines.",
            "TEI’s electro-hydraulic track drill rigs are self-contained units that only require an external power source, which reduces noise and exhaust fumes and removes the need for bulky hydraulic hoses in the drilling area."
          ],
